den's launch sheet (#11): what launching a Job will do, then what it did.
Lines are pre-wrapped by Rust (`ui::launch`); each has a label column and text.

Line styles: strong (title), step (teal: the Next Step), caution (amber, always
with a glyph in the text), good (success, always with a glyph in the text),
input (the prompt field), input_active (the prompt field while typing into it),
muted, plain. Colours are engine sentinels (see frame.crepus).

--- LaunchSheet
div w-full h-full flex-col bg-[#aa0002] px-2 pt-1
  div h-[1] text-[#aa000a] "{sheet_label}"
  div h-[1]
  for item in lines
    div h-[1] flex-row
      span w-[12] text-[#aa000a] "{label}"
      if {is_strong}
        span flex-1 font-bold text-[#aa0006] "{text}"
      else if {is_step}
        span flex-1 font-bold text-[#aa0009] "{text}"
      else if {is_caution}
        span flex-1 text-[#aa000f] "{text}"
      else if {is_good}
        span flex-1 text-[#aa000d] "{text}"
      else if {is_input_active}
        span flex-1 bg-[#aa0003] text-[#aa0006] "{text}"
      else if {is_input}
        span flex-1 bg-[#aa0001] text-[#aa0005] "{text}"
      else if {is_muted}
        span flex-1 text-[#aa0007] "{text}"
      else
        span flex-1 text-[#aa0005] "{text}"
  div flex-1
